INT. ST. VINCENT'S - FOURTH FLOOR CORRIDOR - NIGHT

Fluorescent hum. A gurney wheel squeaks somewhere unseen.

Kim, 40s, charge nurse, stands at the station with a chart. Kip, 20s, orderly, mops in slow circles nearby. A visitor sleeps in a chair, mouth open.

Marguerite Voss, 50s, attorney in a wet trench coat, strides in with a leather folio.

MARGUERITE
I need the patient in 412. Now.

KIM
Visiting hours ended at nine.

MARGUERITE
He signed a statement tonight. I need it witnessed before--

Ozzie, 30s, night nurse, they/them, appears from a doorway, pale, pen still in hand.

OZZIE
Nobody's in 412. They went down at ten.

KIP
Went down where?

KIM
Ozzie, what do you mean, went down?

MARGUERITE
Then who signed this?

She lifts the page. Wet ink. Fresh.

A call light CHIMES. 412.

All four look down the hall. The door is open.

Dr. Hale, 60, in a rumpled white coat, steps out of 412. He wipes his hands on a towel. He does not look at them.

DR. HALE
(soft)
He's resting.

The lights flicker. Out. On.

The sleeping visitor is gone. The chair still rocks.
